# `$isPlainInstanceOf(object, Bare)` WHERE THE CLASS HAS NO PUBLIC FIELD. A plain object laid between an object and the prototype of its class is taken: the cell keeps its bit clear, and what is done to the link later ends guards alone.
# So whoever passes by the bit asks a guard of the class as well. The question asked the guards of its fields' names, and a class without one asked none: it now always asks the guard of the side.
# class Bare { #n = 1; read() { return this.#n; } }
# function ask(object: unknown): string { return $isPlainInstanceOf(object, Bare) ? "plain" : "-"; }      in a file of the library
# const made = new Bare();
# print(ask(made));
# change(made, Bare);
# print(ask(made), ask(new Bare()));
# print((made as any).read?.());
